 cbits←pic AlignPic(image style pxsize);pad;bkg
⍝ Align image-bits within pxsize⍴ full picture using style

 :If 2∊style
     :Section   ⍝ ***** Initial bitmap is tiled to fill the image
         cbits←pxsize↑⊃⍪/⊃,/(⌈pxsize÷⍴image)⍴⊂image ⍝ Just do it explicitly
     :EndSection

 :ElseIf 4∊style
     :Section   ⍝ ***** Initial bitmap is scaled to fill the image
        ⍝ We're going to use the object's own Bitmap to compute this for us - it's going to be overwritten anyway
         pic ##.##.∆WS'CBits'image ⍝ Place the original-size pixels in the Bitmap
         pic ##.##.∆WS'Size'pxsize ⍝ Let Dyalog rescale it to fit
         cbits←pic ##.##.∆WG'CBits' ⍝ Retrieve/return the final scaled image
     :EndSection
 :Else
     :Section   ⍝ ***** Initial bitmap is unscaled and centered in the image (truncate to maximum imagesize first)
         cbits←(pxsize⌊⍴image)↑image ⍝ Truncate oversized images before centering
         bkg←256⊥⌽⊃pic._Owner ⎕VGET⊂'_color_'((3⍴240)⍬) ⍝ Background color to use
         pad←2÷⍨pxsize-⍴cbits
         cbits⍪⍨←bkg⍴⍨⌊pad[1],2⊃⍴cbits ⍝ Top-pad
         cbits⍪←bkg⍴⍨⌈pad[1],2⊃⍴cbits ⍝ Bottm-pad
         cbits,⍨←bkg⍴⍨⌊pad[2],⍨1⊃⍴cbits ⍝ Left-pad
         cbits,←bkg⍴⍨⌈pad[2],⍨1⊃⍴cbits ⍝ Right-pad
     :EndSection
 :EndIf
